  "details": "Hey,\n\nRecently there was a gross missenterpretation of the Vrchat TOS in regards with password sharing and uploading avatars for other people as a lot of people misunderstood this TOS rule as you would no longer be allowed to upload for someone else.\n\nAn announcement was sent in the vrchat discord clarifying this, but this made me think.\n\nWhat if every account had a sort of upload token you use to upload avatars in unity instead of username and password?\n\nThis could help with keeping people's accounts safe AND give the community the ability to have someone help them upload avatars without sharing any information.\n\nCould make it so you can pick from using a login and password OR use an avatar upload token",
